== 1.4 random non-increasing profiles: is  Ntilde_{L+1}(j) = 1 + sum_{i<=j} Ntilde_L(i) ? ==
   4000 random profiles, 33567 (profile,j) checks: violations of the identity = 0
   violations of the inductive lemma A'_{j+1}=A_{j+1}+A'_j : 0
   -> the T1 law is a general identity for ANY non-increasing bound profile with l_0>=1.
      It uses NO property of beta, of the Sturmian word, or of the window.
== 1.5 control: non-monotone profiles (note: the model's l is ALWAYS non-increasing;
        a non-monotone input is silently reduced to its running minimum, so this is a
        consistency check, not an independent test of monotonicity) ==
   1761 non-monotone profiles tested, 0 violate the identity (they reduce to their
   running minimum, which is non-increasing -> monotonicity is WLOG, not an extra hypothesis)
